# Text files are stored with LF in the repository and checked out in the
# platform's native form. Without this, Windows working copies (CRLF) staged
# whole files as changed: every Python file in HEAD is LF, and committing a
# CRLF copy turns a two-line fix into a diff of every line. text=auto only
# normalizes what git detects as text; binaries are left untouched.
* text=auto

# Shell scripts get bind-mounted straight into Linux containers (see
# instraclustr/docker-compose.yml's vault-init/cassandra-init entrypoints),
# so they MUST check out with LF line endings regardless of platform --
# a CRLF line ending breaks `set -eu`/`set -euo pipefail` with
# "illegal option -" the moment a container's shell tries to run it
# (the trailing \r gets read as part of the option string). This bit us
# for real with instraclustr/vault-init.bash: git checkout on Windows
# doesn't normally rewrite line endings (core.autocrlf isn't set here),
# but something along the way had left the working-tree copy as CRLF
# while the committed blob was correctly LF -- this file guarantees it
# can't happen again regardless of local git config or editor settings.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.bash text eol=lf
